{"slug":"/students/subjects/biology/regulation/nervous-coordination/","source":"students/subjects/biology/regulation/nervous-coordination.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Nervous Coordination - Biology","description":"","subject":"biology","body":"<!-- Header -->\n    <nav class=\"bg-white shadow-sm fixed top-0 w-full z-50\">\n        <div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4\">\n            <div class=\"flex justify-between h-16 items-center\">\n                <div class=\"flex items-center\">\n                    <a href=\"/students/subjects/biology/regulation/\" class=\"text-purple-600 hover:text-purple-800 mr-4\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>\n                    </a>\n                    <h1 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900\">Nervous Coordination</h1>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"flex items-center space-x-4\">\n                    <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 hidden sm:block\">\n                        Progress: <span id=\"progressPercent\">0%</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"w-24 sm:w-32 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full\">\n                        <div id=\"progressBar\" class=\"h-2 bg-purple-500 rounded-full transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </nav>\n\n    <!-- Main Content -->\n    <main class=\"pt-20 pb-8 px-4 max-w-5xl mx-auto\">\n        <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n        <div class=\"bg-purple-50 border-l-4 border-purple-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Describe the structure and function of neurons</li>\n                <li>• Explain how nerve impulses are transmitted</li>\n                <li>• Differentiate between sensory, relay, and motor neurons</li>\n                <li>• Describe the reflex arc and synaptic transmission</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 1: The Nervous System Overview -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n                The Nervous System\n            </h2>\n            \n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">The <strong>nervous system</strong> is a complex network of cells that coordinates the body's actions and responses to stimuli. It works alongside the endocrine system to maintain homeostasis.</p>\n            \n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -brain mr-2\" data-mi=\"psychology\">psychology</span>Central Nervous System (CNS)</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• <strong>Brain</strong> - control center</li>\n                        <li>• <strong>Spinal cord</strong> - information highway</li>\n                        <li>• Processes information and makes decisions</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -network-wired mr-2\" data-mi=\"lan\">lan</span>Peripheral Nervous System (PNS)</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• All nerves outside the CNS</li>\n                        <li>• <strong>Sensory neurons</strong> - carry signals TO CNS</li>\n                        <li>• <strong>Motor neurons</strong> - carry signals FROM CNS</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 2: Structure of a Neuron -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n                Structure of a Neuron (Nerve Cell)\n            </h2>\n\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">A <strong>neuron</strong> is the basic unit of the nervous system. It is specialized for transmitting electrical signals called nerve impulses.</p>\n\n            <!-- Neuron Diagram -->\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n                <svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 250\" class=\"w-full max-w-2xl mx-auto\">\n                    <!-- Cell body -->\n                    <ellipse cx=\"150\" cy=\"125\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"40\" fill=\"#e9d5ff\" stroke=\"#9333ea\" stroke-width=\"2\"></ellipse>\n                    <text x=\"150\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cell Body</text>\n                    \n                    <!-- Nucleus -->\n                    <circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"125\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#c4b5fd\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\" stroke-width=\"1\"></circle>\n                    <text x=\"150\" y=\"129\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#5b21b6\" font-size=\"8\">Nucleus</text>\n                    \n                    <!-- Dendrites -->\n                    <line x1=\"100\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#9333ea\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line>\n                    <line x1=\"100\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#9333ea\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line>\n                    <line x1=\"100\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#9333ea\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line>\n                    <line x1=\"110\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#9333ea\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line>\n                    <text x=\"60\" y=\"60\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" font-size=\"10\">Dendrites</text>\n                    \n                    <!-- Axon -->\n                    <line x1=\"200\" y1=\"125\" x2=\"480\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"#9333ea\" stroke-width=\"4\"></line>\n                    <text x=\"340\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" font-size=\"11\">Axon</text>\n                    \n                    <!-- Myelin sheath -->\n                    <rect x=\"250\" y=\"115\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"1\" rx=\"3\"></rect>\n                    <rect x=\"300\" y=\"115\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"1\" rx=\"3\"></rect>\n                    <rect x=\"350\" y=\"115\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"1\" rx=\"3\"></rect>\n                    <rect x=\"400\" y=\"115\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"1\" rx=\"3\"></rect>\n                    <text x=\"340\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b45309\" font-size=\"10\">Myelin Sheath</text>\n                    \n                    <!-- Axon terminals -->\n                    <line x1=\"480\" y1=\"125\" x2=\"510\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#9333ea\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line>\n                    <line x1=\"480\" y1=\"125\" x2=\"510\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"#9333ea\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line>\n                    <line x1=\"480\" y1=\"125\" x2=\"510\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#9333ea\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line>\n                    <circle cx=\"515\" cy=\"100\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#9333ea\"></circle>\n                    <circle cx=\"515\" cy=\"125\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#9333ea\"></circle>\n                    <circle cx=\"515\" cy=\"150\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#9333ea\"></circle>\n                    <text x=\"540\" y=\"130\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" font-size=\"10\">Axon</text>\n                    <text x=\"540\" y=\"142\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" font-size=\"10\">Terminals</text>\n                    \n                    <!-- Direction arrow -->\n                    <path d=\"M 60 200 L 540 200\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrowhead2)\"></path>\n                    <defs>\n                        <marker id=\"arrowhead2\" markerWidth=\"10\" markerHeight=\"7\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"3.5\" orient=\"auto\">\n                            <polygon points=\"0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></polygon>\n                        </marker>\n                    </defs>\n                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"220\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"10\">Direction of nerve impulse</text>\n                </svg>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-3 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-purple-400\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800\">Dendrites</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Short, branched extensions that receive signals from other neurons and carry them toward the cell body.</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-indigo-50 p-3 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-indigo-400\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-800\">Cell Body (Soma)</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Contains the nucleus and organelles. Integrates incoming signals and generates nerve impulses.</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-violet-50 p-3 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-violet-400\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-violet-800\">Axon</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Long extension that carries nerve impulses away from the cell body. Can be up to 1 meter long!</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-3 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-yellow-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800\">Myelin Sheath</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Fatty insulating layer around some axons. Produced by Schwann cells. Speeds up impulse transmission.</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-pink-50 p-3 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-pink-400\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-pink-800\">Axon Terminals</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Branched endings that release neurotransmitters to pass signals to the next neuron or effector.</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 3: Types of Neurons -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n                Types of Neurons\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2 text-center\">Sensory Neuron</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm text-center mb-2\">Detects stimuli and sends signals TO the CNS</p>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-xs space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• Long dendrite, short axon</li>\n                        <li>• Found in sense organs</li>\n                        <li>• Carries info from receptors</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-purple-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-700 mb-2 text-center\">Relay Neuron</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm text-center mb-2\">Connects sensory and motor neurons in CNS</p>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-xs space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• Short dendrites and axon</li>\n                        <li>• Found in brain and spinal cord</li>\n                        <li>• Processes information</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-2 text-center\">Motor Neuron</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm text-center mb-2\">Carries signals FROM CNS to effectors</p>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-xs space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• Short dendrites, long axon</li>\n                        <li>• Connects to muscles/glands</li>\n                        <li>• Causes action/response</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 4: The Synapse -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n                Synaptic Transmission\n            </h2>\n\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">A <strong>synapse</strong> is the junction between two neurons or between a neuron and an effector. Signals are transmitted across synapses using chemicals called neurotransmitters.</p>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n                <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 text-sm\">\n                    <li><strong>Impulse arrives</strong> at the axon terminal of the presynaptic neuron</li>\n                    <li><strong>Calcium channels open</strong>, allowing Ca²⁺ ions to enter</li>\n                    <li><strong>Synaptic vesicles fuse</strong> with the membrane and release neurotransmitters</li>\n                    <li><strong>Neurotransmitters diffuse</strong> across the synaptic cleft</li>\n                    <li><strong>Neurotransmitters bind</strong> to receptors on the postsynaptic membrane</li>\n                    <li><strong>New impulse generated</strong> in the postsynaptic neuron</li>\n                    <li><strong>Neurotransmitters broken down</strong> by enzymes or reabsorbed</li>\n                </ol>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -flask mr-2\" data-mi=\"science\">science</span>Common Neurotransmitters</h4>\n                <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                    <li>• <strong>Acetylcholine</strong> - at neuromuscular junctions, causes muscle contraction</li>\n                    <li>• <strong>Dopamine</strong> - involved in pleasure, reward, and movement</li>\n                    <li>• <strong>Serotonin</strong> - mood regulation, sleep, appetite</li>\n                    <li>• <strong>Adrenaline</strong> - \"fight or flight\" response</li>\n                </ul>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 5: Reflex Arc -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n                The Reflex Arc\n            </h2>\n\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">A <strong>reflex arc</strong> is the neural pathway that controls a reflex action - a rapid, automatic response that doesn't require conscious thought.</p>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n                <div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-2 text-center\">\n                    <div class=\"bg-white px-3 py-2 rounded-lg border border-purple-300\">\n                        <p class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-purple-700\">1. Stimulus</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">e.g., hot object</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <span class=\"mi -arrow-right text-purple-400\" data-mi=\"arrow_forward\">arrow_forward</span>\n                    <div class=\"bg-blue-100 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg border border-blue-300\">\n                        <p class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-blue-700\">2. Receptor</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">detects stimulus</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <span class=\"mi -arrow-right text-purple-400\" data-mi=\"arrow_forward\">arrow_forward</span>\n                    <div class=\"bg-indigo-100 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg border border-indigo-300\">\n                        <p class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-700\">3. Sensory Neuron</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">to spinal cord</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <span class=\"mi -arrow-right text-purple-400\" data-mi=\"arrow_forward\">arrow_forward</span>\n                    <div class=\"bg-violet-100 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg border border-violet-300\">\n                        <p class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-violet-700\">4. Relay Neuron</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">in CNS</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <span class=\"mi -arrow-right text-purple-400\" data-mi=\"arrow_forward\">arrow_forward</span>\n                    <div class=\"bg-green-100 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg border border-green-300\">\n                        <p class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-green-700\">5. Motor Neuron</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">to effector</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <span class=\"mi -arrow-right text-purple-400\" data-mi=\"arrow_forward\">arrow_forward</span>\n                    <div class=\"bg-orange-100 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg border border-orange-300\">\n                        <p class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-orange-700\">6. Effector</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">muscle/gland</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <span class=\"mi -arrow-right text-purple-400\" data-mi=\"arrow_forward\">arrow_forward</span>\n                    <div class=\"bg-red-100 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg border border-red-300\">\n                        <p class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-red-700\">7. Response</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">e.g., pull away</p>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-green-50 border-l-4 border-green-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Why Are Reflexes Important?</h4>\n                <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                    <li>• <strong>Speed:</strong> Bypasses the brain for faster response</li>\n                    <li>• <strong>Protection:</strong> Helps avoid injury (e.g., pulling hand from hot object)</li>\n                    <li>• <strong>Automatic:</strong> No conscious thought needed</li>\n                </ul>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 6: Video -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">6</span>\n                Video: The Nervous System\n            </h2>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                <div class=\"video-container\">\n                    <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/vK8qk1FWZDU\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Practice Problems -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-purple-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n                Practice Questions\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. What is the function of the myelin sheath?</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            The myelin sheath <strong>insulates the axon</strong> and <strong>speeds up nerve impulse transmission</strong>. It allows impulses to \"jump\" between gaps (Nodes of Ranvier) in a process called saltatory conduction.\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. State three differences between sensory and motor neurons.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            <table class=\"w-full text-xs\">\n                                <tbody><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"text-left py-1\">Sensory Neuron</th><th class=\"text-left py-1\">Motor Neuron</th></tr>\n                                <tr class=\"border-b\"><td>Long dendrite</td><td>Short dendrites</td></tr>\n                                <tr class=\"border-b\"><td>Carries signals TO CNS</td><td>Carries signals FROM CNS</td></tr>\n                                <tr class=\"border-b\"><td>Cell body off to side</td><td>Cell body at end</td></tr>\n                                <tr><td>Connects to receptors</td><td>Connects to effectors</td></tr>\n                            </tbody></table>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. Explain why reflex actions are faster than voluntary actions.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            Reflex actions are faster because:\n                            <ul class=\"list-disc list-inside mt-1\">\n                                <li>The impulse doesn't travel to the brain for processing</li>\n                                <li>Only the spinal cord is involved (shorter pathway)</li>\n                                <li>No conscious decision-making is required</li>\n                                <li>Fewer synapses to cross</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-50 to-violet-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-purple-200 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n                <li>• The nervous system controls rapid responses through electrical impulses</li>\n                <li>• Neurons have dendrites (receive), cell body (process), and axon (transmit)</li>\n                <li>• Three types: sensory (to CNS), relay (in CNS), motor (from CNS)</li>\n                <li>• Synapses use neurotransmitters to transmit signals between neurons</li>\n                <li>• Reflex arcs provide rapid, automatic protective responses</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Navigation -->\n        <div class=\"flex justify-between items-center mt-8\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/biology/regulation/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-900\">\n                <span class=\"mi -chevron-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_left\">chevron_left</span>Previous\n            </a>\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/biology/regulation/hormonal-coordination/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 bg-purple-500 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-purple-600\">\n                Next: Hormones<span class=\"mi -chevron-right ml-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_right\">chevron_right</span>\n            </a>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    \n\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"bg-gray-50 min-h-screen","bodyStyle":"","css":["@keyframes fade-in-up {\n            from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px); }\n            to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }\n        }\n        .animate-fade-in-up { animation: fade-in-up 0.5s ease-out forwards; }\n        .section-card {\n            background: white;\n            border-radius: 12px;\n            padding: 1.5rem;\n            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;\n            box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\n            border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;\n        }\n        .video-container {\n            position: relative;\n            width: 100%;\n            padding-bottom: 56.25%;\n            height: 0;\n            overflow: hidden;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            background: #f9fafb;\n        }\n        .video-container iframe {\n            position: absolute;\n            top: 0; left: 0;\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 100%;\n            border: none;\n        }"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}